# PROVENANCE: measured, not generated. Every response byte below was captured
# from a genuine DESFire EV1 8K over PC/SC by a PC/SC capture tool
# and is used here as an expectation for our emulator. As with the other
# hardware_genuine_*.vec files, this vector is the opposite of the rest
# of the corpus: the others were recorded from the reference engine, so they
# pin what we decided; this one pins what the silicon does. A mismatch here is
# either a real divergence or a difference we can justify in writing, never a
# vector to be re-recorded from our engine.
#
# Card: UID 04304622216A80, hardware 1.0, software 1.4, storage 8K. Formatted
# with FormatPICC under the all-zero PICC test key, then provisioned with
# a synthetic structure whose every key is a published test key. That is what
# makes an authenticated capture safe to commit and replayable: no key material
# enters the tree, and our engine derives the same session key from the same
# pinned nonces.
#
# RndA is the fixed constant the recorder uses; RndB is the card's, recovered
# by decrypting its first authentication frame with the test key and
# pinned here with inject-random so our engine offers the same challenge.
# What this vector is for: the octets each CreateApplication consumed, measured:
#    1. 1 DES/2K3DES key, iso-fid+df-name   128 octets,  4 blocks
#    2. 1 DES/2K3DES key, iso-fid            96 octets,  3 blocks
#    3. 14 AES keys                         288 octets,  9 blocks
#    4. 12 AES keys                         256 octets,  8 blocks
#    5. 11 AES keys                         288 octets,  9 blocks
#    6. 8 AES keys                          192 octets,  6 blocks
#    7. 5 AES keys                          160 octets,  5 blocks
#    8. 4 AES keys                          128 octets,  4 blocks
#    9. 3 AES keys                          160 octets,  5 blocks
#   10. 2 AES keys                           96 octets,  3 blocks
#   11. 1 AES key                            96 octets,  3 blocks
#   12. 14 3K3DES keys                      384 octets, 12 blocks
#   13. 12 3K3DES keys                      384 octets, 12 blocks
#   14. 5 3K3DES keys                       192 octets,  6 blocks
#   15. 4 3K3DES keys                       160 octets,  5 blocks
#   16. 1 3K3DES key                         96 octets,  3 blocks
#   17. 14 DES/2K3DES keys                  320 octets, 10 blocks
#   18. 12 DES/2K3DES keys                  256 octets,  8 blocks
#   19. 11 DES/2K3DES keys                  224 octets,  7 blocks
#   20. 8 DES/2K3DES keys                   192 octets,  6 blocks
#   21. 5 DES/2K3DES keys                   160 octets,  5 blocks
#   22. 4 DES/2K3DES keys                   128 octets,  4 blocks
#   23. 3 DES/2K3DES keys                    96 octets,  3 blocks
#   24. 2 DES/2K3DES keys                    96 octets,  3 blocks
#   25. 1 DES/2K3DES key                     96 octets,  3 blocks
# An application with no keys was answered 9E.

name: genuine EV1 8K, memory each application consumes, by key type and count, the same cases in reverse order
origin: physical-card
uid: 04304622216A80
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-key-len: 16
picc-generation: EV1
picc-storage: 8192

scan
# Free memory after FormatPICC, the starting point for every delta below.
exchange native-apdu 906E000000 => 001F009100 tolerance 0+3 512
#   (tolerance above: free space after a format)
#
# OPEN DIVERGENCE, card versus engine: how free memory is accounted.
#
# Our engine charges an application nothing. The card charges each one
# for its directory entry and keys, as the table in the header records,
# so the difference grows past any tolerance within a few applications
# and the steps below are recorded unexecuted. Restore them when the
# engine accounts for application and key overhead.
#
#
# An application with 1 DES/2K3DES key, iso-fid+df-name.
#   exchange native-apdu 90CA00000E2810E00F2118E1D276000085012800 => 9100
#   exchange native-apdu 906E000000 => 801E009100 tolerance 0+3 512
#   (tolerance above: 1 DES/2K3DES key, iso-fid+df-name consumed 128 octets)
#
# An application with 1 DES/2K3DES key, iso-fid.
